\# Architecture Document: GraphOne / Frontier AI Data Pipeline



\## PAGE 1: System Overview \& Architecture

\### 1.1 High-Level Design

The pipeline is built on a decoupled, asynchronous architecture designed to ingest, process, and enrich AI ecosystem data. The workflow progresses linearly through discrete phases: Data Acquisition -> Enrichment -> Extraction -> Entity Resolution -> Validation.



\### 1.2 Component Interaction

\* Sources: APIs (StartupDB, ZOIPI, arXiv, GitHub, Ashby) and feeds (News).

\* Async Adapters: aiohttp and requests gather data concurrently.

\* Storage: Data is stored as raw CSVs before downstream processing to prevent data loss.



\---



\## PAGE 2: LLM Orchestration, Entity Resolution, \& Data Quality

\### 2.1 Multi-Tier LLM Orchestration

\* Primary Engine: Gemini (gemini-3.6-flash).

\* Fallback Concept: Groq Llama -> DeepSeek (architected but currently dormant to ensure tested reliability).

\* Execution: Uses Pydantic for structured JSON output. Implements intelligent chunking (starting at 5000 chars, reducing to 500 on 413 Payload Errors) to prevent data truncation.



\### 2.2 Deterministic Entity Resolution

\* Cleanses the startup `name` field using strict deterministic rules: Unicode normalization, lowercase conversion, punctuation stripping, suffix removal (Inc, LLC, Corp), and canonical formatting.



\### 2.3 Data Quality \& No-Hallucination

\* Strict adherence to source truth. Missing publication dates (e.g., in jobs/news) are dropped rather than faked. LLM system instructions strictly forbid hallucinated entities.



\---



\## PAGE 3: Scaling, Anti-Bot, \& Fault Tolerance

\### 3.1 Scaling to 500,000+ Records

\* Horizontal Scaling: The decoupled architecture supports independent worker pools for each crawler.

\* Async I/O: Non-blocking execution prevents freezing during massive network requests.

\* Task Queues: The codebase is structured so crawlers can be easily dropped into Celery/Redis queues without changing core application logic.



\### 3.2 Anti-Bot Strategy

\* Exclusively uses official APIs, RSS feeds, or permitted endpoints.

\* Adheres strictly to security rules: no bypassing of CAPTCHAs, Cloudflare, or DataDome.



\### 3.3 Fault Tolerance (Retry Logic)

\* LLM and HTTP calls implement exponential backoff with jitter for HTTP 408, 429, 500, 502, 503, and 504 errors, ensuring resilience against rate limits and server timeouts.

